A small IP stack for RSTS/E V10.1 that runs as an ordinary detached job on
the RSTS/E Ethernet portal interface (XE:, DEUNA/DELUA). No monitor changes.

  - TFTP server (RFC 1350): read and write, 512-byte blocks, files in FTP$:
  - ARP and ping (ICMP echo)
  - DHCP client: address, mask, router and lease from your network; the
    host name sent is the DECnet node name (or HOSTNAME)
  - Coexists with DECnet/E: start DECnet first and give its node address
    (DECNET area.node name) in TCPIP$:TCPIP.INI

Files (TCPIP$: = SY:[0,91]):
  TFTPD.TSK   the server          TCPIP.INS  start-up file
  TCPIP.INI   settings            *.C *.H *.MAC  sources

Start at boot: add  $ @SY:[0,91]TCPIP.INS  to [0,1]START.COM.
Use: tftp <address>, then get/put; file names are plain RSTS names
(e.g. HELLO.C); files read back are padded with NULs to a 512-byte block.

Known limits: one transfer at a time; no IP fragments; TFTP options
(RFC 2347) are not supported; netascii is sent as stored (CR LF).
